 "notes": "Manual, the whole repo (several small apps: stringsvc1-4, addsvc, apigateway, profilesvc, shipping). Expected = every route registration read in the source. Misses: package-level net/http registration http.Handle(\"/uppercase\", h) on the default mux (default-mux-function — http.DefaultServeMux.Handle is extracted, http.Handle is not); gorilla builder chains with the method first, r.Methods(\"POST\").Path(\"/profiles/\").Handler(h) (route-chain); the gateway mounts addsvc under /addsvc with r.PathPrefix(\"/addsvc\").Handler(http.StripPrefix(...)) (prefix-other-file) — both found since H2b item 4 (2026-10-16), and /sum, /concat stay because addsvc's main serves the same handler (http.Serve). Wrong: mux.Handle(\"/booking/v1/\", booking.MakeHandler(...)) is a subtree mount and comes out as the route ANY /booking/v1 (mount-as-route). Calls: go-kit clients take the method in httptransport.NewClient(\"GET\", tgt, enc, dec) and set the path in the request encoder (req.URL.Path = \"/profiles/\" + id) — request-encoder; or on the URL (u.Path = \"/paths\") — url-object-builder. None was extracted until H2b's Go calls (2026-10-16); since then both are. The /uppercase client (stringsvc3, and the gateway's factory) is a GET (it was listed as POST). Added then: addsvc's client, copyURL(u, \"/sum\") with the path a parameter of the helper that sets it, and the gateway's stringsvcFactory(ctx, \"GET\", \"/count\") — url-from-helper. Since the v2 cheap fixes (2026-10-15): http.Handle on the default mux is a route, and a ServeMux pattern ending in / is a mount, not a route.",
